import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse('{"title":"Retro — the $leaf: auto-compose seam + the batch_norm LHS law","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Retro — the `$leaf:` auto-compose seam + the `batch_norm` LHS law","type":"retro","date":"2026-10-18T00:00:00.000Z"},"headers":[],"relativePath":"graphopt/project/retros/leaf-compose-seam.md","filePath":"vendored/graphopt/project/retros/leaf-compose-seam.md"}'),a={name:`graphopt/project/retros/leaf-compose-seam.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="retro-—-the-leaf-auto-compose-seam-the-batch-norm-lhs-law" tabindex="-1">Retro — the <code>$leaf:</code> auto-compose seam + the <code>batch_norm</code> LHS law <a class="header-anchor" href="#retro-—-the-leaf-auto-compose-seam-the-batch-norm-lhs-law" aria-label="Permalink to “Retro — the $leaf: auto-compose seam + the batch_norm LHS law”">​</a></h1><p><strong>Closes</strong>: the two named limits in <code>project/adrs/0012-tensor-derives.md</code> / <code>GOALS.md</code> §&quot;Still open&quot; — (a) <code>$leaf:</code> rules can&#39;t auto-compose in <code>meta.synthesize_rules</code> (the <code>@i:</code> placeholder machinery was attr-only), and (b) no law LHS named <code>batch_norm</code> (<code>weightspace-fold.md</code> gate 5 — content, not capability).</p><h2 id="item-1-—-term-level-placeholders" tabindex="-1">Item 1 — term-level placeholders <a class="header-anchor" href="#item-1-—-term-level-placeholders" aria-label="Permalink to “Item 1 — term-level placeholders”">​</a></h2><p>The ADR&#39;s resolver seam, landed as the <em>twin</em> of the attr machinery rather than a grammar widening. A <code>$leaf:</code>-produced RHS term metavar now travels through composition exactly the way a derived attr does:</p><ul><li><code>_synthesizable</code> admits a rule whose RHS term metavar is unbound when <code>rule.derive</code> can produce it (the attr clause&#39;s mirror; the earlier blanket <code>return False</code> was the measured refusal).</li><li><code>_fire_guarded</code> keeps <em>every</em> derive output symbolic under the <code>@i:</code> namespace — <code>&quot;$attr:&quot;</code> keys become <code>&quot;@i:X&quot;</code> attr placeholders, bare (<code>$leaf:</code>) keys become <code>&quot;@i:X&quot;</code> <em>leaf</em> placeholders — and records the concrete value in <code>conc</code> either way.</li><li><code>_concretize_attrs</code> resolves placeholder <em>leaves</em> (not just attr values) so a second parent&#39;s guards/derives see the minted <code>Param</code>/ <code>Const</code>, never the string.</li><li><code>_compose_guards</code> namespaces term outputs identically: <code>eff1[&quot;@1:X&quot;]</code> lets a <code>pat2</code> entry reference the parent&#39;s derived leaf, and the composite <code>derive</code> emits <code>out[&quot;@i:X&quot;]</code> — the instantiate-time resolution the ADR asked for, re-running the parent&#39;s spec through the pushed <code>TensorAlgebra</code> (<code>source</code>/<code>ops</code>/ <code>mint</code>) per firing. Nothing is baked in — the earlier silent bake of a concrete <code>Param</code> into a derived RHS (reachable only by cheating <code>_synthesizable</code>) is structurally impossible now.</li><li><code>_rhs_derive_placeholders</code> scans leaf positions too, and <code>_validate_candidate</code> admits <code>@i:</code>-prefixed RHS term metavars when the candidate derives — unresolved placeholders veto the firing, which validation measures as refusal.</li></ul><p>Nested composition namespaces correctly by construction (<code>&quot;@1:@2:X&quot;</code>), the same convention attr placeholders already use.</p><p><strong>Measured.</strong> <code>tests/test_batch_norm_expand.py</code>: <code>synthesize_rules([mark→marked(a,eps:$leaf:), marked(u,k)→sink(u,k)], [mark(v)])</code> emits a candidate whose RHS carries <code>&quot;@1:eps&quot;</code> and whose firing lands <code>Const(2.0)</code> — before the seam the parent was filtered by <code>_synthesizable</code> (refusal count 1 → 0). The twin seats are both covered (<code>&quot;@2:eps&quot;</code> when the <code>$leaf:</code> rule is r2), and <code>batch_norm_expand</code> itself — a real <code>$leaf:</code> rule — composes.</p><h2 id="item-2-—-the-batch-norm-law-family" tabindex="-1">Item 2 — the <code>batch_norm</code> law family <a class="header-anchor" href="#item-2-—-the-batch-norm-law-family" aria-label="Permalink to “Item 2 — the batch_norm law family”">​</a></h2><p><code>laws/tensor.py</code> gains <code>BATCH_NORM_RULES</code> — three arity variants of the eval-mode expansion <code>batch_norm → γ·((x−μ)·rsqrt(σ²+ε)) + β</code> (affine / weight-only / affine-free — the operand arities aten exports after dropping <code>None</code>s). Everything is data:</p><ul><li><code>cond</code>: <code>training=False</code> (eval only — training computes batch stats, different math), concrete <code>x</code>/<code>rm</code>, channel-extent and per-channel shape agreement, <code>2 ≤ rank(x) ≤ 6</code>.</li><li><code>dspec</code>: <code>CH = (1,) + shape(rm) + take(ones, rank(x)−2)</code> — the <code>(1, C, 1…)</code> broadcast target derived per-rank, one law covering ranks 2–6 (<code>take</code> is Python-clamped; the <code>≤ 6</code> guard is what keeps a longer rank from minting a short target silently); <code>$leaf:EPS</code> mints <code>Const(eps)</code> through the scalar side of ADR 0012&#39;s channel — no tensor algebra needed.</li></ul><p><strong>Held out of DEFAULT</strong> as an opt-in list — the admission floor (the guarded sweep the promoted laws cleared) has not run; <code>ALL_RULES</code> is unchanged, extraction behavior for every existing caller unchanged. The fused member stays cheapest under extraction (priced 4 &lt; the ~7-pass spelled subgraph), so the family is optionality, not a regression, wherever it is opted in.</p><p><strong>Measured.</strong> fp64-exact vs <code>F.batch_norm</code> through the torch bridge (max|Δ| = 7.3e-13 on (2,6,4,4)); <code>training=True</code>, stats/x channel mismatch, rank-1 and rank-7 inputs, and unshaped <code>x</code> all decline — the strictness contract, never a fabricated member.</p><h2 id="what-stays-open" tabindex="-1">What stays open <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-stays-open" aria-label="Permalink to “What stays open”">​</a></h2><ul><li>The conv+BN <em>weight fold</em> itself: <code>W&#39; = W·γ·rsqrt(σ²+ε)</code>, <code>b&#39; = (b−μ)·scale + β</code> — now reachable (stats are visible as terms, <code>tval</code>+<code>mint</code> can mint the folded <code>Param</code>), but the law is un-authored — it wants the tensor-valued <code>$leaf:</code> parents to auto-compose, which this seam enables; a follow-up measurement should try <code>synthesize_rules</code>/<code>dspec_synth</code> over a real conv→batch_norm seed rather than hand-writing it.</li><li><code>DEFAULT</code> admission for <code>BATCH_NORM_RULES</code> — pending the guarded sweep (off this box&#39;s budget).</li><li>The mint-determinism contract remains documented-not-enforced (ADR 0012 (b)).</li></ul>`,14)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};